package com.app.pegsolitaire.data.db

import androidx.room.Entity
import androidx.room.PrimaryKey
import com.app.pegsolitaire.data.ProgressPersistenceKeys

/**
 * One **solved** play, recorded once when it is solved (PGSA-06, D-06).
 *
 * This is the append-only history behind the skill achievements: unlike
 * [LevelResultEntity], which keeps a single best row per `(mode, levelId)`, replaying
 * a level appends a *second* row here — `(mode, levelId)` is deliberately **not**
 * unique — which is exactly why the key is a surrogate autogenerated [id] rather than
 * the natural pair. A "solved without a single hint" or "solved three levels in a row
 * with the last peg on target" question can only be answered from per-play rows, not
 * from a merged best.
 *
 * [mode] and [levelId] reuse [LevelResultEntity]'s conventions verbatim — the same
 * `ProgressPersistenceKeys.MODE_*` literals and the same Classic-id-or-Challenge-number
 * text — so the aggregate queries added in plan 12-06 can filter and join both tables
 * on identical values.
 *
 * Two storage facts that the queries in 12-06 depend on: [lastPegOnTarget] is a Kotlin
 * `Boolean` and therefore stores as `INTEGER NOT NULL`, so SQL predicates must compare
 * it against `1`/`0` and never against `true`/`false`; and there is deliberately **no**
 * retention or pruning policy (D-06 discretion) — thousands of rows is well within what
 * SQLite handles and discarding history would make an aggregate unrecomputable.
 *
 * Like [LevelResultEntity] this is the flat storage shape only: it imports no `:domain`
 * type, keeping the domain module free of Room annotations (QUAL-01).
 */
@Entity(tableName = ProgressPersistenceKeys.TABLE_PLAY_SESSION)
data class PlaySessionEntity(
    /** Surrogate key; rows are append-only, so replays never collide. */
    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
    /** `"classic"` or `"challenge"` — see `ProgressPersistenceKeys.MODE_*`. */
    val mode: String,
    /** Classic catalog id, or the Challenge level number rendered as text. */
    val levelId: String,
    /** Star rating earned by *this* play, 0-3 (not the best ever). */
    val stars: Int,
    /** Score earned by this play. */
    val score: Int,
    /** Wall-clock solve time of this play, in milliseconds. */
    val elapsedMs: Long,
    /** Hints consumed during this play. */
    val hintsUsed: Int,
    /** Undos used during this play. */
    val undosUsed: Int,
    /** Whether the final peg finished on the board's target hole; stored as `INTEGER`. */
    val lastPegOnTarget: Boolean,
    /** Epoch millis this play was solved. */
    val finishedAt: Long,
)
